<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Every string the user can see.

  They used to live in the Kotlin, which is why lint reported 48 SetTextI18n
  warnings and why the app could only ever speak English — to a user whose
  family are named גבע, דני and אמא.

  Conventions here: %1$s and %1$d are positional on purpose, because word order
  changes between languages and a translator has to be able to move them.
  Anything counted is a <plurals>, because "1 photos" is wrong in English and
  the rule is different again in Hebrew, which has a dual.
-->
